          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5352bae511a2e71f471bf3e569b8a10194da8854",
          "message": "docs(readme-gate): correct stale ADVISORY framing + add pre-PR readme-template guidance to agent defs (sq-bhgve) [OPUS-4.8] (#979)\n\nThe readme-template check was PROMOTED advisory→HARD under sq-8ic6\n(docs-quality.yml runs it with --enforce; the ci-summary aggregator gates on\nthe no-advisory-token job \"readme-template (template)\"). But agents kept\ntripping it (PRs #967/#969/#975/#977 all blocked) because the guidance was\nstale/missing:\n\n- scripts/check-readme-template.py header still said \"STATUS: ADVISORY … only\n  REPORTS … without blocking\" — stale + actively misleading now that it GATES.\n  Header comment + --advisory/--enforce help + the GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY text now\n  state it is a HARD/REQUIRED gate. LOGIC UNCHANGED (self-test + --enforce still\n  green across all 36 READMEs); only comments/help/display strings touched.\n- .claude/agents/sparq-site.md + sparq-ci-infra.md gained a mandatory pre-PR\n  readme-template step (≤120 lines + 🚀 Quickstart / ✨ Features / 📚 Learn more\n  + License, or a ≤30-line <!-- internal-stub --> stub for publish=false; prefer\n  rustdoc over an over-cap README). sparq-rust-feature.md + sparq-docs.md already\n  carry equivalent guidance on origin/main, so they are unchanged.\n\nDOC-ONLY. Ref sq-8ic6.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
