          "distinct": true,
          "id": "dbe4ad898f1c6921805b75eb012aafb6b5b5858c",
          "message": "test(sparq-conformance): wire W3C JSON-LD 1.1 compact suite into the ratchet (sq-3uos5) (#969)\n\n* test(sparq-conformance): wire W3C JSON-LD 1.1 compact suite into the ratchet (sq-3uos5) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nExtends the JSON-LD conformance ratchet (sq-oy1f.2, epic sq-oy1f) with the W3C\n`compact` category, gating sparq's native hand-rolled Compaction Algorithm\n(`graph_to_jsonld_compact`, serialize-rdf) behind the opt-in `jsonld-suite`\nfeature alongside the existing toRdf + fromRdf lanes.\n\nPipeline (the REAL compaction path, oxjsonld self-reparse oracle):\n  1. parse each `jld:CompactTest` input `.jsonld` -> RDF via oxjsonld;\n  2. load that RDF into a sparq Graph (named graphs preserved);\n  3. compact against the case `@context` (top-level manifest `context` member,\n     the inner `@context` of the sibling `*-context.jsonld`);\n  4. re-parse the compacted document and require `reparse(compact(D, ctx)) === D`\n     (lossless compaction — the same round-trip invariant fromRdf uses), NOT a\n     byte diff against the suite `expect.jsonld`.\n\nHonest measured baseline at the pinned w3c/json-ld-api revision: compact\n163 pass / 58 fail / 25 skip. COMPACT_FLOOR = 163 (the actual pass count, not\ninflated). The 58 below-floor cases are real writer divergences (the\n`@type:@id`-coerced-key-vs-plain-string IRI confusion; `@graph`/`@index`/`@id`/\n`@language` multi-value container round-trips the hand-rolled writer does not yet\nreproduce), to RISE later. The 25 SKIP are negatives sparq's TOTAL compaction\ndoes not raise, JSON-LD-1.0-only cases, non-inline/remote `@context`, and\nempty-RDF inputs (SKIP is not PASS).\n\nOracle caveat (documented in the runner + README + SKILL): the comparison is\noxjsonld self-reparse equivalence, so the `@reverse` double-inversion /\nnon-string-language strict-third-party (pyld) faithfulness gap is NOT caught here\nand is tracked separately under sq-oy1f.\n\n  * `compact` GRADUATED out of the runner's NOT_IMPLEMENTED_CATS bucket (frame\n    stays deferred, sq-oy1f.6);\n  * central scoreboard `SUITES` gains the `compact` FeatureGatedCrateTest row\n    (floor 163), kept in lock-step by the `scoreboard_floors.rs` floor-sync guard\n    (new CRATE_LOCAL_FLOORS tuple + render assertion);\n  * `ci.yml` `jsonld-conformance` job adds the `^TOTAL compact ` grep ratchet\n    (COMPACT_FLOOR=163) mirroring the toRdf/fromRdf belt-and-braces gate (the\n    runner's own assert is the primary gate);\n  * no fetch-script change — the compact manifest is already vendored by the\n    same pinned clone.\n\nGates (both feature states): `cargo test -p sparq-conformance --features\njsonld-suite --test jsonld_suite` GREEN at compact >= 163; `cargo test -p\nsparq-conformance` (feature OFF) self-skip GREEN; `cargo test -p\nsparq-conformance --test scoreboard_floors` GREEN; `cargo clippy --workspace\n--all-targets --all-features -D warnings` clean; `RUSTDOCFLAGS=-D warnings cargo\ndoc --workspace --no-deps --all-features` clean. New code rustfmt-clean (the\nfile's pre-existing intentionally-deferred reformat left untouched).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(sparq-conformance): tighten stub README under 30-line cap (sq-3uos5) [OPUS-4.8]\n\nThe readme-template gate (scripts/check-readme-template.py --enforce) flagged\ncrates/sparq-conformance/README.md as \"declared a stub but 35 lines (stub\ntarget: <=30)\". The crate carries the explicit `<!-- internal-stub -->`\ndirective, so the hard 30-line cap applies; this PR's compact-lane additions\npushed it to 35.\n\nCondensed prose (35 -> 26 lines) WITHOUT losing the compact-lane substance:\nmerged the three-binary bullet list into one sentence, shortened the\ncompact-lane paragraph to its essential claim, and folded the dev-only-harness\nnote + fetch-script list together. Preserved: the internal-stub directive, the\ntitle, that the opt-in `jsonld-suite` feature drives toRdf + fromRdf + compact,\nthat the compact lane (sq-3uos5) parses each `jld:CompactTest`, runs Compaction\nagainst the case `@context`, and requires lossless self-reparse\n(`reparse(compact(D, ctx)) ≡ D`), and the `## License` section.\n\nLocal checks green: check-readme-template --enforce (0 deviations) + --self-test;\ncargo build/clippy -p sparq-conformance (default + jsonld-suite, -D warnings);\ncargo test -p sparq-conformance --features jsonld-suite (compact ratchet holds\nat floor 163).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
